{"name":"Roastery","hex":"#692302","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"roastery","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place where meat, coffee, etc. is roasted."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roastery"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coffee roasting","blocks":[{"text":"Roasting coffee transforms the chemical and physical properties of green coffee beans into roasted coffee products. The roasting process produces the characteristic flavor of coffee by causing the green coffee beans to change in taste. Unroasted beans contain similar if not higher levels of acids, protein, sugars, and caffeine as those that have been roasted, but lack the taste of roasted coffee beans due to the Maillard and other chemical reactions which occur during roasting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Miele%2C_IFA_2018%2C_Berlin_%28P1070083%29.jpg/330px-Miele%2C_IFA_2018%2C_Berlin_%28P1070083%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee_roasting"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Coffee_roaster_from_Baghdad%2C_15th_century.jpg/330px-Coffee_roaster_from_Baghdad%2C_15th_century.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Coffee_roaster_from_Baghdad%2C_15th_century.jpg/330px-Coffee_roaster_from_Baghdad%2C_15th_century.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"15th-century coffee roasting pan and stirring spoon from Baghdad","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACoffee_roaster_from_Baghdad%2C_15th_century.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Free_standing_tin_coffee_roaster_-_DPLA_-_ab92df8478ed695bac532e581df00ba5_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Free_standing_tin_coffee_roaster_-_DPLA_-_ab92df8478ed695bac532e581df00ba5_%28cropped